"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[89869],{589869:e=>{e.exports="# Writing Unit Tests for Databricks Python Code\n\nUse this skill when the user asks you to generate, write, or create unit tests for Python code, including PySpark and Spark Declarative Pipelines code.\n\n## Test Framework Requirements\n\n**IMPORTANT: You MUST use pytest as the testing framework. Do NOT use unittest.**\n\n- Use pytest fixtures for setup/teardown instead of unittest's setUp/tearDown.\n- Use pytest assertions (`assert` statements) instead of `self.assertEqual`, `self.assertTrue`, etc.\n- Use `pytest.raises` for exception testing instead of `self.assertRaises`.\n\n## General Guidelines\n\n- Prefer using PySpark's built-in dataframe testing utilities for comparing expected vs actual output.\n- Do not create a SparkSession for non-pipeline tests. For Spark Declarative Pipelines tests, create/obtain an isolated session via the mandatory `test_spark` fixture imported from `pyspark.pipelines.testing`.\n- Write code as if you are generating a new Python file — include all imports needed to run the file.\n- Give a short explanation of what each test verifies; do not repeat the guidelines back to the user.\n- When creating test files within a pipelines project using the `createPipelineFile` tool, always exclude the test file from the pipeline by setting the `includeInPipeline` parameter to false.\n\n## Identifying Spark Declarative Pipelines Code\n\nSpark Declarative Pipelines code can be identified by:\n\n- Decorators like `@dp.table`, `@dp.materialized_view`, `@dp.streaming_table`, `@dp.view` (from `pyspark.pipelines` or `pyspark import pipelines as dp`).\n- **`@dp.table` decorators that use `spark.readStream` define streaming tables** — these are Spark Declarative Pipelines code and must be tested with TestPipeline, not a direct SparkSession.\n- SQL with `CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW` or `CREATE STREAMING TABLE`.\n\nIf the source code is Spark Declarative Pipelines code, follow the Spark Declarative Pipelines specific guidance in [`reference-spark-declarative-pipelines.md`](reference-spark-declarative-pipelines.md).\n\nFor non-pipeline PySpark code, write standard pytest tests using PySpark's built-in testing utilities.\n"}}]);
